STEP 11 — Understand little endian

The binary is little endian.

So:

02 00       = 0x0002
33 00       = 0x0033
34 00       = 0x0034
6f 00 00 00 = 0x0000006f
81 00 00 00 = 0x00000081


STEP 12 — Identify the fields

>>> 0x2110

53 30 75 4c
= magic = S0uL

02 00
= version = 0x0002

33 00
= width = 0x0033

34 00
= height = 0x0034

00 00
= padding

6f 00 00 00
= data_length = 0x0000006f

81 00 00 00
= checksum = 0x00000081


STEP 13 — Derive the first 4 key bytes

Magic:

53 30 75 4c

Transformation:

key[i] = magic[i] ^ 0x5A

Calculation:

53 ^ 5A = 09
30 ^ 5A = 6A
75 ^ 5A = 2F
4C ^ 5A = 16

Result:

key[0..3] = 09 6A 2F 16


STEP 14 — Derive key bytes from version

Version:

02 00

Little endian:

version_lo = 02
version_hi = 00

Transformation:

key[4] = version_hi + 0x11
key[5] = version_lo + 0x11

Calculation:

00 + 11 = 11
02 + 11 = 13

Result:

key[4..5] = 11 13


STEP 15 — Derive key bytes from width

Width:

33 00

Transformation:

key[6] = rol8(width_lo, 3)
key[7] = rol8(width_hi, 3)

Calculation:

0x33 = 00110011

ROL 3:

00110011
   |
   v
10011001

10011001 = 0x99

Therefore:

key[6] = 99
key[7] = 00

Result:

key[6..7] = 99 00


STEP 16 — Derive key bytes from height

Height:

34 00

Version:

02 00

Transformation:

key[8] = height_lo ^ version_lo
key[9] = height_hi ^ version_hi

Calculation:

34 ^ 02 = 36
00 ^ 00 = 00

Result:

key[8..9] = 36 00


STEP 17 — Derive key bytes from data length

Data length:

6f 00 00 00

Transformation:

key[i] = data_length[i] ^ 0xA5

Calculation:

6F ^ A5 = CA
00 ^ A5 = A5
00 ^ A5 = A5
00 ^ A5 = A5

Result:

key[10..13] = CA A5 A5 A5


STEP 18 — Derive key bytes from checksum

Checksum:

81 00 00 00

Use low byte:

81

For key[14]:

Swap nibbles:

81
>>
18

Therefore:

key[14] = 18

For key[15]:

ROL 81 by 1:

10000001
   |
   v
00000011

00000011 = 03

Therefore:

key[15] = 03


