STEP 24 — Understand the decoding

The decoding operation is:

cipher byte
    |
    v
ROR by 3
    |
    v
XOR with key
    |
    v
plaintext

The key has 16 bytes.

stage2.dat has 25 bytes.

Therefore the key repeats:

byte 0  -> key[0]
byte 1  -> key[1]
...
byte 15 -> key[15]
byte 16 -> key[0]
byte 17 -> key[1]


STEP 25 — Create the decoder

$ nano solve.py

Use:

def ror8(b, n):
    n %= 8
    return ((b >> n) | (b << (8 - n))) & 0xff


key = bytes.fromhex(
    "096a2f16111399003600caa5a5a51803"
)

with open("stage2.dat", "rb") as f:
    ciphertext = f.read()

plaintext = bytes(
    ror8(c, 3) ^ key[i % 16]
    for i, c in enumerate(ciphertext)
)

print(plaintext)


STEP 26 — Run the decoder

$ python3 solve.py

The script applies:

ROR 3
+
XOR with repeating 16-byte key

and produces the decoded plaintext.


